<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Nov new car sales up 18.4 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>S.African Nov new car sales up 18.4 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African new cars sales fell 14.9 percent to 23,677 units in November from 27,814 in October, but rose 18.4 percent compared with the 19,995 units sold in November 1995, latest National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of South Africa figures show.</p>
<p>    Detailed Sales data:	   Nov 96  Oct 96  Nov 95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars	     23,677  27,814  19,995</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles    10,963  12,158  10,566</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles   496     671     380</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles    664     730     667</p>
<p>    TOTAL:			     35,800  41,373  31,608</p>
<p>Individual manufacturer car sales:</p>
<p>Toyota 9,433, Samcor 6,522, Volkswagen 5,615, Delta 4,899, Nissan 3,760, Mercedes-Benz 2,889, BMW 1,424, Daewoo 623, Land Rover SA 272, MAN 94, Iveco 91, Chrysler 82, Tyco 41, Scania 20, Dacia 12, Freightliner 10, ERF 7, AAD 4, Subaru 2.</p>
<p>					    Jan-Nov 96    Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars		232,158	 219,280</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles     121,208	 119,297</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	5,111	   3,901</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 7,608	   7,220</p>
<p>    TOTAL:				366,085	 349,698</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
